<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>BAM Engine</title><link>https://bamengine.org/</link><description>Recent content on BAM Engine</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 09 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://bamengine.org/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>BAM Engine 0.6.0 — Vectorized Market Matching</title><link>https://bamengine.org/posts/2026-03-bam-engine-060/</link><pubDate>Mon, 09 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/posts/2026-03-bam-engine-060/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BAM Engine 0.6.0&lt;/strong&gt; consolidates two parallel market-matching implementations
into a single vectorized path, delivering ~30% faster simulations.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>BAM Engine 0.5.1 and the Launch of bamengine.org</title><link>https://bamengine.org/posts/2026-03-launch/</link><pubDate>Wed, 04 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/posts/2026-03-launch/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;We are excited to announce &lt;strong&gt;BAM Engine 0.5.1&lt;/strong&gt; and the launch of
&lt;a href="https://bamengine.org"&gt;bamengine.org&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>About</title><link>https://bamengine.org/about/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/about/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;BAM Engine is a high-performance Python implementation of the BAM
(Bottom-Up Adaptive Macroeconomics) model from
&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-88-470-1971-3"&gt;Macroeconomics from the Bottom-up&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;
(Delli Gatti et al., 2011). It simulates three agent types — households,
firms, and banks — interacting across labor, credit, and consumption goods
markets. Macroeconomic dynamics emerge entirely from individual agent
decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="history"&gt;History&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#history" title="Link to this heading"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BAM Engine began as an MSc thesis at the Department of Informatics,
University of Piraeus, Greece, with the goal of producing a modern,
extensible Python implementation of the BAM model.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Baseline Scenario</title><link>https://bamengine.org/gallery/baseline/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/gallery/baseline/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The baseline scenario reproduces section 3.9.1 of Delli Gatti et al. (2011)
with default parameters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://bamengine.org/images/gallery-baseline.png" alt="Baseline scenario output"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Eight panels: Real GDP, unemployment rate, inflation, productivity vs real
wage, Phillips curve, Okun curve, Beveridge curve, and firm size distribution.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run this yourself:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;
 &lt;pre class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;bamengine&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;bam&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sim&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;bam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Simulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;init&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;n_periods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;show&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See the &lt;a href="https://bam-engine.readthedocs.io/en/latest/auto_examples/basic/example_baseline_scenario.html"&gt;full example&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Benchmark List</title><link>https://bamengine.org/benchmarks/list/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/benchmarks/list/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Flat table of all validation metrics across scenarios. Use the toolbar to
filter by release, scenario, or metric group, and click column headers to sort.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="benchmark-list" id="benchmark-list"
 data-green-score-threshold="0.85"
 data-yellow-score-threshold="0.8"
 data-green-pass-threshold="0.97"
 data-yellow-pass-threshold="0.96"&gt;
 &lt;div class="benchmark-loading" id="bl-loading"&gt;Loading benchmark data...&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="benchmark-empty" id="bl-empty" style="display:none;"&gt;
 No benchmark data available yet.
 &lt;/div&gt;

 &lt;div id="bl-content" style="display:none;"&gt;
 
 &lt;div class="benchmark-toolbar"&gt;
 &lt;div class="toolbar-group"&gt;
 &lt;label&gt;Release:&lt;/label&gt;
 &lt;select id="bl-release"&gt;&lt;/select&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="toolbar-group"&gt;
 &lt;label&gt;Scenarios:&lt;/label&gt;
 &lt;div class="checkbox-group" id="bl-scenarios"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="toolbar-group"&gt;
 &lt;label&gt;Groups:&lt;/label&gt;
 &lt;div class="checkbox-group" id="bl-groups"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="toolbar-group"&gt;
 &lt;label&gt;Search:&lt;/label&gt;
 &lt;input type="text" id="bl-search" placeholder="Filter metrics..."&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;

 
 &lt;div class="benchmark-row-count" id="bl-row-count"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

 
 &lt;div class="benchmark-table-wrap"&gt;
 &lt;table class="benchmark-table"&gt;
 &lt;thead&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;th data-col="scenario"&gt;Scenario &lt;span class="sort-arrow"&gt;&amp;#9650;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th data-col="group"&gt;Group &lt;span class="sort-arrow"&gt;&amp;#9650;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th data-col="metric"&gt;Metric &lt;span class="sort-arrow"&gt;&amp;#9650;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th data-col="mean_score"&gt;Score &lt;span class="sort-arrow"&gt;&amp;#9650;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th data-col="pass_rate"&gt;Pass Rate &lt;span class="sort-arrow"&gt;&amp;#9650;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th data-col="mean_value"&gt;Value &amp;plusmn; Std &lt;span class="sort-arrow"&gt;&amp;#9650;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th data-col="weight"&gt;Weight &lt;span class="sort-arrow"&gt;&amp;#9650;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th data-col="score_delta"&gt;Recent Change &lt;span class="sort-arrow"&gt;&amp;#9650;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th data-col="changed_at"&gt;Changed At &lt;span class="sort-arrow"&gt;&amp;#9650;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/thead&gt;
 &lt;tbody id="bl-tbody"&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;
 &lt;/table&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
(function() {
'use strict';




var root = document.getElementById('benchmark-list');
var THRESHOLD_GREEN_SCORE = parseFloat(root.dataset.greenScoreThreshold);
var THRESHOLD_YELLOW_SCORE = parseFloat(root.dataset.yellowScoreThreshold);
var THRESHOLD_GREEN_PASS = parseFloat(root.dataset.greenPassThreshold);
var THRESHOLD_YELLOW_PASS = parseFloat(root.dataset.yellowPassThreshold);
var DATA_BASE = '\/data\/validation\/';
var COLOR_THRESHOLD = 5; 
var HIDE_THRESHOLD = 1; 
var GITHUB_BASE = 'https://github.com/kganitis/bam-engine';

var SCENARIO_NAMES = {
 baseline: 'Baseline',
 growth_plus: 'Growth+',
 buffer_stock: 'Buffer-Stock'
};




var manifest = null;
var cachedData = {};
var allRows = [];
var sortCol = 'scenario';
var sortAsc = true;
var checkedScenarios = {};
var checkedGroups = {};




function scoreStatusClass(score) {
 if (score &gt;= THRESHOLD_GREEN_SCORE) return 'status-green';
 if (score &gt;= THRESHOLD_YELLOW_SCORE) return 'status-yellow';
 return 'status-red';
}

function passStatusClass(passRate) {
 if (passRate &gt;= THRESHOLD_GREEN_PASS) return 'status-green';
 if (passRate &gt;= THRESHOLD_YELLOW_PASS) return 'status-yellow';
 return 'status-red';
}




async function loadManifest() {
 try {
 var resp = await fetch(DATA_BASE + 'manifest.json');
 if (!resp.ok) throw new Error('No manifest found');
 manifest = await resp.json();
 } catch (e) {
 document.getElementById('bl-loading').style.display = 'none';
 document.getElementById('bl-empty').style.display = 'block';
 return;
 }

 if (!manifest.runs || manifest.runs.length === 0) {
 document.getElementById('bl-loading').style.display = 'none';
 document.getElementById('bl-empty').style.display = 'block';
 return;
 }

 
 var select = document.getElementById('bl-release');
 for (var i = 0; i &lt; manifest.runs.length; i++) {
 var run = manifest.runs[i];
 var opt = document.createElement('option');
 opt.value = i;
 var label = run.tag || run.commit_short;
 var date = (run.commit_date || run.timestamp).split('T')[0];
 opt.textContent = label + ' (' + date + ')';
 select.appendChild(opt);
 }

 
 var scenarioDiv = document.getElementById('bl-scenarios');
 for (var key of Object.keys(SCENARIO_NAMES)) {
 checkedScenarios[key] = true;
 var lbl = document.createElement('label');
 var cb = document.createElement('input');
 cb.type = 'checkbox';
 cb.checked = true;
 cb.value = key;
 cb.addEventListener('change', function() {
 checkedScenarios[this.value] = this.checked;
 renderTable();
 });
 lbl.appendChild(cb);
 lbl.appendChild(document.createTextNode(' ' + SCENARIO_NAMES[key]));
 scenarioDiv.appendChild(lbl);
 }

 document.getElementById('bl-loading').style.display = 'none';
 document.getElementById('bl-content').style.display = '';

 await loadRelease();
}

async function loadResultFile(filename) {
 if (cachedData[filename]) return cachedData[filename];
 try {
 var resp = await fetch(DATA_BASE + filename);
 if (!resp.ok) throw new Error('Failed to load ' + filename);
 var data = await resp.json();
 cachedData[filename] = data;
 return data;
 } catch (e) {
 console.error('Failed to load result file:', filename, e);
 return null;
 }
}

async function loadRelease() {
 var select = document.getElementById('bl-release');
 var idx = parseInt(select.value, 10);
 var run = manifest.runs[idx];
 allRows = [];

 
 var allFilesToFetch = [];
 for (var ri = 0; ri &lt; manifest.runs.length; ri++) {
 var r = manifest.runs[ri];
 for (var sk of Object.keys(r.scenarios)) {
 allFilesToFetch.push(r.scenarios[sk].file);
 }
 }
 await Promise.all(allFilesToFetch.map(loadResultFile));

 
 var allMetrics = [];
 for (var ri = 0; ri &lt; manifest.runs.length; ri++) {
 var lookup = {};
 var r = manifest.runs[ri];
 for (var sk of Object.keys(r.scenarios)) {
 var d = cachedData[r.scenarios[sk].file];
 if (!d) continue;
 for (var mn of Object.keys(d.metrics)) {
 lookup[sk + ':' + mn] = d.metrics[mn];
 }
 }
 allMetrics.push(lookup);
 }

 
 var scenarioKeys = Object.keys(run.scenarios);
 var groupSet = {};

 for (var i = 0; i &lt; scenarioKeys.length; i++) {
 var scenarioKey = scenarioKeys[i];
 var data = cachedData[run.scenarios[scenarioKey].file];
 if (!data) continue;

 var groupNames = data.group_display_names || {};

 for (var metricName of Object.keys(data.metrics)) {
 var m = data.metrics[metricName];
 var groupKey = m.group || 'OTHER';
 var groupDisplay = groupNames[groupKey] || groupKey;
 groupSet[groupKey] = groupDisplay;

 
 var change = findSignificantChange(idx, scenarioKey, metricName, allMetrics);

 allRows.push({
 scenario: scenarioKey,
 scenarioDisplay: SCENARIO_NAMES[scenarioKey] || scenarioKey,
 group: groupKey,
 groupDisplay: groupDisplay,
 metric: metricName,
 mean_score: m.mean_score,
 pass_rate: m.pass_rate,
 mean_value: m.mean_value,
 std_value: m.std_value,
 weight: m.weight,
 scoreDelta: change ? change.delta : null,
 scoreDeltaPct: change ? change.deltaPct : null,
 changedAtDate: change ? change.atDate : null,
 changedAtCommits: change ? change.commitRange : null,
 prevRef: change ? change.prevRef : null,
 afterRef: change ? change.afterRef : null
 });
 }
 }

 
 var groupDiv = document.getElementById('bl-groups');
 groupDiv.innerHTML = '';
 checkedGroups = {};
 var sortedGroups = Object.keys(groupSet).sort();
 for (var gk of sortedGroups) {
 checkedGroups[gk] = true;
 var lbl = document.createElement('label');
 var cb = document.createElement('input');
 cb.type = 'checkbox';
 cb.checked = true;
 cb.value = gk;
 cb.addEventListener('change', function() {
 checkedGroups[this.value] = this.checked;
 renderTable();
 });
 lbl.appendChild(cb);
 lbl.appendChild(document.createTextNode(' ' + groupSet[gk]));
 groupDiv.appendChild(lbl);
 }

 renderTable();
}




function findSignificantChange(idx, scenarioKey, metricName, allMetrics) {
 var key = scenarioKey + ':' + metricName;
 for (var i = idx; i &lt; manifest.runs.length - 1; i++) {
 var current = allMetrics[i][key];
 var prev = allMetrics[i + 1][key];
 if (!current || !prev) continue;
 if (prev.mean_score === 0) continue;
 var delta = current.mean_score - prev.mean_score;
 var deltaPct = delta / prev.mean_score * 100;
 if (Math.abs(deltaPct) &gt;= HIDE_THRESHOLD) {
 var afterRun = manifest.runs[i];
 var prevRun = manifest.runs[i + 1];
 return {
 delta: delta,
 deltaPct: deltaPct,
 atDate: (afterRun.commit_date || afterRun.timestamp).split('T')[0],
 commitRange: prevRun.commit_short + '...' + afterRun.commit_short,
 prevRef: prevRun.tag || prevRun.commit_short,
 afterRef: afterRun.tag || afterRun.commit_short
 };
 }
 }
 return null;
}




function getFilteredRows() {
 var search = document.getElementById('bl-search').value.toLowerCase();
 return allRows.filter(function(row) {
 if (!checkedScenarios[row.scenario]) return false;
 if (!checkedGroups[row.group]) return false;
 if (search &amp;&amp; row.metric.toLowerCase().indexOf(search) === -1) return false;
 return true;
 });
}

function compareValues(a, b) {
 if (a &lt; b) return -1;
 if (a &gt; b) return 1;
 return 0;
}

function sortRows(rows) {
 var col = sortCol;
 var asc = sortAsc;
 rows.sort(function(a, b) {
 var va, vb;
 switch (col) {
 case 'scenario': va = a.scenarioDisplay; vb = b.scenarioDisplay; break;
 case 'group': va = a.groupDisplay; vb = b.groupDisplay; break;
 case 'metric': va = a.metric; vb = b.metric; break;
 case 'mean_score': va = a.mean_score; vb = b.mean_score; break;
 case 'pass_rate': va = a.pass_rate; vb = b.pass_rate; break;
 case 'mean_value': va = a.mean_value; vb = b.mean_value; break;
 case 'weight': va = a.weight; vb = b.weight; break;
 case 'score_delta':
 va = a.scoreDeltaPct !== null ? Math.abs(a.scoreDeltaPct) : -1;
 vb = b.scoreDeltaPct !== null ? Math.abs(b.scoreDeltaPct) : -1;
 break;
 case 'changed_at': va = a.changedAtDate || ''; vb = b.changedAtDate || ''; break;
 default: va = a.metric; vb = b.metric;
 }
 var cmp = compareValues(va, vb);
 return asc ? cmp : -cmp;
 });
 return rows;
}




function renderTable() {
 var filtered = getFilteredRows();
 var sorted = sortRows(filtered);

 document.getElementById('bl-row-count').textContent =
 'Showing ' + sorted.length + ' of ' + allRows.length + ' metrics';

 var tbody = document.getElementById('bl-tbody');
 var html = '';
 for (var row of sorted) {
 var scoreClass = scoreStatusClass(row.mean_score);
 var passClass = passStatusClass(row.pass_rate);
 
 var deltaCell;
 if (row.scoreDeltaPct !== null) {
 var sign = row.scoreDelta &gt;= 0 ? '+' : '';
 var absPct = Math.abs(row.scoreDeltaPct);
 var deltaClass;
 if (absPct &gt;= COLOR_THRESHOLD) {
 deltaClass = row.scoreDelta &gt;= 0 ? 'change-positive' : 'change-negative';
 } else {
 deltaClass = 'change-neutral';
 }
 deltaCell = '&lt;td class="' + deltaClass + '"&gt;' +
 sign + row.scoreDeltaPct.toFixed(1) + '% (' +
 sign + row.scoreDelta.toFixed(3) + ')&lt;/td&gt;';
 } else {
 deltaCell = '&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;';
 }

 
 var changedCell;
 if (row.changedAtDate &amp;&amp; row.prevRef) {
 var compareUrl = GITHUB_BASE + '/compare/' + row.prevRef + '...' + row.afterRef;
 changedCell = '&lt;td class="col-changed-at"&gt;' + row.changedAtDate +
 ' &lt;a class="commit-range" href="' + compareUrl + '" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;' +
 row.changedAtCommits + '&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;';
 } else {
 changedCell = '&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;';
 }

 
 var metricLink = '\/benchmarks\/validation\/?scenario=' +
 encodeURIComponent(row.scenario) + '&amp;metric=' + encodeURIComponent(row.metric);

 html +=
 '&lt;tr&gt;' +
 '&lt;td class="col-scenario"&gt;' + row.scenarioDisplay + '&lt;/td&gt;' +
 '&lt;td&gt;' + row.groupDisplay + '&lt;/td&gt;' +
 '&lt;td class="col-metric"&gt;&lt;a href="' + metricLink + '"&gt;' + row.metric + '&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;' +
 '&lt;td class="' + scoreClass + '"&gt;' + row.mean_score.toFixed(3) + '&lt;/td&gt;' +
 '&lt;td class="' + passClass + '"&gt;' + (row.pass_rate * 100).toFixed(1) + '%&lt;/td&gt;' +
 '&lt;td&gt;' + row.mean_value.toFixed(4) + ' &amp;plusmn; ' + row.std_value.toFixed(4) + '&lt;/td&gt;' +
 '&lt;td&gt;' + row.weight + '&lt;/td&gt;' +
 deltaCell +
 changedCell +
 '&lt;/tr&gt;';
 }
 tbody.innerHTML = html;

 
 var ths = document.querySelectorAll('.benchmark-table th');
 for (var th of ths) {
 var col = th.dataset.col;
 var arrow = th.querySelector('.sort-arrow');
 if (col === sortCol) {
 th.classList.add('sorted');
 arrow.innerHTML = sortAsc ? '&amp;#9650;' : '&amp;#9660;';
 } else {
 th.classList.remove('sorted');
 arrow.innerHTML = '&amp;#9650;';
 }
 }
}

function sortBy(col) {
 if (sortCol === col) {
 sortAsc = !sortAsc;
 } else {
 sortCol = col;
 sortAsc = true;
 }
 renderTable();
}




document.getElementById('bl-release').addEventListener('change', function() {
 loadRelease();
});

document.getElementById('bl-search').addEventListener('input', function() {
 renderTable();
});


var ths = document.querySelectorAll('.benchmark-table th[data-col]');
for (var th of ths) {
 th.addEventListener('click', function() {
 sortBy(this.dataset.col);
 });
}




loadManifest();

})();
&lt;/script&gt;</description></item><item><title>Buffer-Stock Consumption</title><link>https://bamengine.org/gallery/buffer-stock/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/gallery/buffer-stock/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The buffer-stock extension (section 3.9.4) replaces the baseline mean-field
MPC with an individual adaptive rule based on buffer-stock saving theory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://bamengine.org/images/gallery-buffer-stock-1.png" alt="Buffer-stock wealth CCDF"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Complementary CDF of household wealth on log-log axes, fitted against
Singh-Maddala, Dagum, and GB2 distributions (Figure 3.8).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run this yourself:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;
 &lt;pre class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;bamengine&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;bam&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;extensions.rnd&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;RND&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;extensions.buffer_stock&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;BUFFER_STOCK&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sim&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;bam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Simulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;init&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;42&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;use&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;RND&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;use&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;BUFFER_STOCK&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;n_periods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;show&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See the &lt;a href="https://bam-engine.readthedocs.io/en/latest/auto_examples/extensions/example_buffer_stock.html"&gt;full example&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Community</title><link>https://bamengine.org/community/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/community/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="contributing"&gt;Contributing&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#contributing" title="Link to this heading"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BAM Engine is not currently accepting external contributions as the project
is part of ongoing thesis work. Once the thesis is submitted, contribution
guidelines will be published.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the meantime, bug reports and feature requests are welcome via the issue
tracker.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Issue tracker:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/kganitis/bam-engine/issues"&gt;github.com/kganitis/bam-engine/issues&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source code:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/kganitis/bam-engine"&gt;github.com/kganitis/bam-engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="related-projects--the-cats-family"&gt;Related Projects — The CATS Family&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#related-projects--the-cats-family" title="Link to this heading"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The BAM model (Delli Gatti et al., 2011) has inspired a family of
implementations and extensions within the CATS (Complex Adaptive Trivial
Systems) lineage.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Documentation</title><link>https://bamengine.org/docs/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/docs/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Growth+ Extension</title><link>https://bamengine.org/gallery/growth-plus/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/gallery/growth-plus/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The Growth+ extension adds R&amp;amp;D investment and endogenous productivity growth
to the baseline model (chapter 3.8).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://bamengine.org/images/gallery-growth-plus-1.png" alt="Growth+ macro dynamics"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Time series with recession bands (GDP, unemployment, inflation,
productivity-wage ratio), Phillips, Okun, and Beveridge curves, and firm
size distribution.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://bamengine.org/images/gallery-growth-plus-2.png" alt="Growth+ financial dynamics"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Output and net-worth growth rate distributions, real interest rate,
bankruptcies, financial fragility, price-clearing ratio, price dispersion,
and equity-sales dispersion.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run this yourself:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;
 &lt;pre class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;bamengine&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;bam&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;extensions.rnd&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;RND&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sim&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;bam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Simulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;init&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;42&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;use&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;RND&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;n_periods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;show&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See the &lt;a href="https://bam-engine.readthedocs.io/en/latest/auto_examples/extensions/example_growth_plus.html"&gt;full example&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Installation</title><link>https://bamengine.org/install/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/install/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="requirements"&gt;Requirements&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#requirements" title="Link to this heading"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python 3.11 or later&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NumPy &amp;gt;= 1.26 (installed automatically)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PyYAML &amp;gt;= 6.0.2 (installed automatically)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="install-with-pip"&gt;Install with pip&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#install-with-pip" title="Link to this heading"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;
 &lt;pre class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;pip install bamengine&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3 id="optional-extras"&gt;Optional extras&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#optional-extras" title="Link to this heading"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;
 &lt;pre class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;pip install bamengine&lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;pandas&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# DataFrame export&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;pip install bamengine&lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;viz&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Matplotlib plotting&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;pip install bamengine&lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;validation&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Validation framework&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;pip install bamengine&lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;extensions&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# All extensions&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;pip install bamengine&lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;dev&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Development dependencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id="install-from-source"&gt;Install from source&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#install-from-source" title="Link to this heading"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;
 &lt;pre class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;git clone https://github.com/kganitis/bam-engine.git
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; bam-engine
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;pip install -e &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;.[dev]&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id="verify"&gt;Verify&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#verify" title="Link to this heading"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;
 &lt;pre class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;bamengine&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;bam&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;bam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;__version__&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Publications &amp; Citations</title><link>https://bamengine.org/publications/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/publications/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;If you use BAM Engine in your research, please cite both the software
and the original BAM model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="citing-the-software"&gt;Citing the Software&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#citing-the-software" title="Link to this heading"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ganitis, K. (2026). &lt;em&gt;BAM Engine: A Modular Python Framework for the BAM
Agent-Based Macroeconomic Model&lt;/em&gt; [Computer software].
&lt;a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17610305"&gt;https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17610305&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;
 &lt;pre class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;@software&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;ganitis2026bamengine&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;{{BAM Engine}: A Modular Python Framework for the {BAM}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; Agent-Based Macroeconomic Model}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;author&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;{Ganitis, Konstantinos}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;year&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;{2026}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;{https://github.com/kganitis/bam-engine}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;doi&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;{10.5281/zenodo.17610305}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;license&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;{MIT}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17610305"&gt;&lt;img src="https://zenodo.org/badge/972128676.svg" alt="DOI"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="citing-the-original-bam-model"&gt;Citing the Original BAM Model&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#citing-the-original-bam-model" title="Link to this heading"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Delli Gatti, D., Desiderio, S., Gaffeo, E., Cirillo, P., &amp;amp; Gallegati, M.
(2011). &lt;em&gt;Macroeconomics from the Bottom-up&lt;/em&gt;. Springer Milano.
&lt;a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-88-470-1971-3"&gt;https://doi.org/10.1007/978-88-470-1971-3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Robustness Analysis</title><link>https://bamengine.org/gallery/robustness/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/gallery/robustness/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Robustness analysis inspired by Section 3.10, using the Growth+ model for
internal validity and sensitivity experiments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://bamengine.org/images/gallery-robustness-1.png" alt="Co-movements at leads and lags"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Internal validity: cross-correlations of unemployment, productivity, price
index, and real wage with GDP across multiple seeds.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://bamengine.org/images/gallery-robustness-2.png" alt="Impulse-response function"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;AR(2) vs AR(1) impulse-response functions for the GDP cyclical component.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://bamengine.org/images/gallery-robustness-3.png" alt="Sensitivity to credit market reach"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sensitivity analysis: co-movement structure under different values of the
credit market reach parameter H.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://bamengine.org/images/gallery-robustness-4.png" alt="Preferential attachment experiment"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Validation Dashboard</title><link>https://bamengine.org/benchmarks/validation/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://bamengine.org/benchmarks/validation/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The validation dashboard tracks two complementary metrics across releases:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Score&lt;/strong&gt; (0–1) — how closely simulation results match calibration targets
from the original BAM model (Delli Gatti et al., 2011). Higher is better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pass rate&lt;/strong&gt; (%) — how consistently random seeds produce valid results.
A seed &amp;ldquo;passes&amp;rdquo; when all its metric scores exceed the tolerance threshold.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Card border colors reflect the &lt;strong&gt;score&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Green&lt;/strong&gt;: score ≥ 0.85 — accurate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Yellow&lt;/strong&gt;: score 0.80–0.85 — marginal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Red&lt;/strong&gt;: score &amp;lt; 0.80 — regression&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pass rate is shown inline with its own coloring (green ≥ 97%, yellow ≥ 96%).&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>